From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenCode <opencode@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] DIAG ONLY: arm the AON watchdog so a hard SoC stop resets

Diagnostic scaffold, compiled in only with KCFLAGS=-DDIAG_WDT_ARM.

Measured on stock (2026-10-30):

  * PSCI is present (the DTBO supplies the node, not the kernel DTB) and a
    deliberate sysrq-c panic reboots the phone in 19 s with a full pstore
    record, so a panic IS observable.  The custom kernel produces neither,
    i.e. it never panics: the SoC simply stops, the way it does on a bus
    access that never completes (same signature as mu300-linux FINDINGS 31m
    on a T760).
  * Nothing arms a watchdog on this firmware.  androidboot.wdten=0 makes
    sprd_pmic_wdt send "watchdog rstoff" (disarm) instead of "watchdog on",
    and sprd_wdt_fiq_probe() enables the AON block but never calls
    watchdog_register_device(), so /sys/class/watchdog is empty and Android's
    watchdogd cannot even open /dev/watchdog.

Consequently a stall is permanent by design.  Arming the AON watchdog here -
after sprd_wdt_fiq_enable() has set up both clocks and NEW_VER_EN - makes the
board reset after 30 s, which is the only way a stopped SoC becomes observable
(the bootloader writes a dump after a watchdog reset).

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/sprd_wdt_fiq.c b/drivers/watchdog/sprd_wdt_fiq.c
--- a/drivers/watchdog/sprd_wdt_fiq.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/sprd_wdt_fiq.c
@@ -364,6 +364,27 @@ static int sprd_wdt_fiq_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	wdt_fiq = wdt;
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, wdt);
 
+#ifdef DIAG_WDT_ARM
+	/*
+	 * DIAG build only (KCFLAGS=-DDIAG_WDT_ARM).
+	 *
+	 * This driver never calls watchdog_register_device(), and stock Android
+	 * passes androidboot.wdten=0, so nothing ever arms a watchdog: a hard
+	 * stop of the SoC (a bus access that never completes) therefore hangs
+	 * for ever with no panic, no reboot and no dump.  Arm the AON watchdog
+	 * here, where its clocks and the new-version bit are already set up by
+	 * sprd_wdt_fiq_enable(), so a stall resets the board after
+	 * DIAG_WDT_TIMEOUT seconds and the bootloader can capture the crash.
+	 */
+	wdt->wdd.timeout = 30;
+	if (sprd_wdt_fiq_set_timeout(&wdt->wdd, 30))
+		pr_err("DIAG: could not set watchdog timeout\n");
+	if (sprd_wdt_fiq_start(&wdt->wdd))
+		pr_err("DIAG: could not start watchdog\n");
+	else
+		pr_info("DIAG: AON watchdog armed, 30 s\n");
+#endif
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
